# No whack-a-mole

The tool must recognize a component on a design it has not seen. A Figma file in this repo is a test, not the product. Real pages will not reuse its words, units, or layer names.

A change to `process/modules/recognize-parts/` or `process/modules/write-bricks/` is a classification of one kind. Name the kind without naming the current section. Recognition asks what structure makes that kind. A word, a unit, a currency, a layer name, or a node id taken from the file that just failed is not a rule.

Forbidden. The next file of the same kind still fails, or a different component that happens to use those tokens is dropped:

- A token list from one file (`đ`, `/th`, `/tháng`, `TB`, `GB`, `MB`, a badge word, a layer name).
- A pixel, a count, or a string length tuned so this section passes.
- A branch that mentions one file key or one node id.

Required before the edit:

1. Write the kind in one sentence that still makes sense if this file is deleted.
2. Add a test whose copy is not the copy of the failing file. A Vietnamese price row is not covered by another Vietnamese price row. Cover the same shape with different words.
3. Keep the existing tests of that kind passing.

If you cannot write that second example, do not edit the rule. Record the miss in `history/notes/gaps.md`.

During a generate run, do not edit `process/` or the theme. The same miss is a note, not a local patch.
